The Smart Warehouse and Inventory Management System is a practical implementation of Data Structures and Algorithms using C.
It demonstrates how Linked Lists, Stacks, Queues, Trees, Graphs, Searching, Sorting, Dynamic Programming, and Greedy Algorithms
can be applied to real-world warehouse operations.

The project combines these concepts into a single warehouse scenario, making it useful not only as an inventory management
application but also as a comprehensive DSA practical project. It demonstrates how the correct selection of data structures and
algorithms can improve inventory organization, order processing, warehouse navigation, and cargo optimization.
